Design acknowledgement
----------------------
Several features added in RVTSS 2.2 were inspired by rvt-mcp by bimwright
(https://github.com/bimwright/rvt-mcp), licensed under the Apache License 2.0:
atomic batches in one transaction group, a read-only mode with a generated
permission allow list, refusing unknown tool arguments with suggestions, a
response-size guard, a one-call health check, a change-impact survey that
reports unchecked relationships explicitly, and the getting-started /
disciplined-change prompt workflows, as well as the scope of the rooms,
materials, annotation, export, MEP, view filter and revision tools.

rvt-mcp is a C# / .NET Revit add-in; RVTSS is IronPython on pyRevit Routes.
The RVTSS implementations were written independently for this code base;
no rvt-mcp source code is included in RVTSS.

